{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.3.181764ab1c","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":3,"group":"bnd-list-1","passage":"<p>The conference speakers included Amara Singh, a marine biologist; Luis Ortega, a ______ Mei Chen, an architect.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["novelist; and","novelist, and","novelist: and","novelist and"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Each item in this list already contains a comma, so <b>semicolons</b> must separate the items to keep them distinct. The pattern set by the first semicolon must continue before “and.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.3.b71d339b1c","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":3,"group":"bnd-list-2","passage":"<p>The band has performed in Austin, Texas; Nashville, ______ Portland, Oregon.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Tennessee, and","Tennessee; and","Tennessee and","Tennessee: and"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Each item in this list already contains a comma, so <b>semicolons</b> must separate the items to keep them distinct. The pattern set by the first semicolon must continue before “and.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.3.ad394437f7","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":3,"group":"bnd-list-10","passage":"<p>The students interviewed Mr. Lee, the principal; Ms. Diaz, the ______ Mr. Owens, the custodian.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["librarian and","librarian; and","librarian, and","librarian: and"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Each item in this list already contains a comma, so <b>semicolons</b> must separate the items to keep them distinct. The pattern set by the first semicolon must continue before “and.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.3.428a98c768","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":3,"group":"bnd-iq-2","passage":"<p>Historians still debate how the ancient city came to be ______ excavations may settle the question.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["abandoned. New","abandoned? New","abandoned? new","abandoned, new"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The first sentence reports a question indirectly (for example, “wondered why” or “asked whether”) instead of asking it directly, so it ends with a <b>period</b>, not a question mark. A comma would create a comma splice."},
{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.3.f65aa2339b","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":3,"group":"bnd-iq-8","passage":"<p>The reporter asked the mayor when the bridge would ______ mayor declined to give a date.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["reopen, the","reopen? the","reopen. The","reopen? The"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The first sentence reports a question indirectly (for example, “wondered why” or “asked whether”) instead of asking it directly, so it ends with a <b>period</b>, not a question mark. A comma would create a comma splice."},
{"id":"g.rw.boundaries.3.70c9e90f62","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":3,"group":"bnd-iq-9","passage":"<p>Nobody knows exactly who built the stone ______ purpose also remains a mystery.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["circle. Its","circle? Its","circle? its","circle, its"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The first sentence reports a question indirectly (for example, “wondered why” or “asked whether”) instead of asking it directly, so it ends with a <b>period</b>, not a question mark. A comma would create a comma splice."}
